.TH "ZOXIDE" "1" "2026-09-02" "" "zoxide"
.SH NAME
\fBzoxide-tidy\fR - repair and clean up database paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zoxide tidy [OPTIONS] [PATHGLOBS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBzoxide tidy\fR performs one or more explicit database maintenance actions.
It can remove paths that are no longer navigable, rewrite stored paths using
their on-disk spelling, and merge different spellings of the same directory.
It never renames filesystem objects.
.sp
At least one action must be selected. PATHGLOBS match original full stored
paths using the same matcher as \fB_ZO_EXCLUDE_DIRS\fR. When no PATHGLOBS are
supplied, \fB'*'\fR selects the whole database.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B -d, --dedupe
Merge textually equivalent entries that the filesystem confirms name the same
directory. Ranks are summed and the newest access time is retained.
.TP
.B --normalize
Rewrite stored paths using the exact spelling of every resolvable filesystem
component. Existing parent components are corrected when a later component is
missing. Symlink aliases are preserved. Exact collisions created by
normalization are merged so scores remain combined.
.TP
.B -p, --prune
Remove paths that no longer resolve to directories, including missing paths,
paths replaced by files, and dangling symlinks. Symlinks resolving to live
directories are retained.
.TP
.B -a, --all
Prune, normalize, and deduplicate, in that order. This option conflicts with the
individual action selectors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -i, --assume-insensitive
For deduplication, skip filesystem identity confirmation and merge every group
that is equivalent under full Unicode case folding plus canonical
normalization. This can merge genuinely distinct directories on case-sensitive
filesystems. Requires \fB--dedupe\fR or \fB--all\fR.
.TP
.B -n, --dry-run
Report what would change without modifying the database.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print help information.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print version information.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Changes and summaries are printed to standard output in deterministic order.
Unexpected filesystem errors leave affected entries unchanged, produce warnings
on standard error, and do not prevent other entries from being processed.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
For any issues, feature requests, or questions, please visit:
